cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use draw.instant in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "draw.instant: real-time on-device Stable Diffusion in the browser via WebGPU kernel fusion"
abstract: >-
  draw.instant runs Stable Diffusion Turbo entirely in the browser on WebGPU,
  targeting interactive ("as-you-type") latency by collapsing the U-Net
  denoising loop from dozens of GPU kernel launches per step into a handful of
  fused WGSL dispatches. It ships a from-scratch WebGPU inference stack — a
  byte-level ONNX parser, a WGSL op-kernel library, and a graph executor — with
  no dependence on ONNX Runtime for the fused path, and a live on-device
  benchmark suite.
type: software
authors:
